= Conclusion {#ch:conclusion}

The answers to the research questions of Chapter @ch:intro are:

1. The cell transmission model becomes a nonlinear state-space model, @eq:state-space,
   that an extended Kalman filter can use, provided the corrected densities are clipped.
2. Floating-car speeds reduce the density error by 31% overall and by 47% in congestion
   (@tab:errors).
3. The filter locates stop-and-go waves within one cell in 92% of the incidents.

Future work should replace the fixed fundamental diagram of @tab:fd with parameters
estimated online, and test the filter on a network with junctions\ix{junction}.
